ERROR 1064 (42000) at line 2: table 't' is a part of cluster 'v1', use 'v1:t'
ERROR 1064 (42000) at line 2: table 'l' is not in any cluster, use just 'l'
t count=4001 l count=0
––– comment –––
Evidence from the loading node 1 and a receiver: the chunk was prepared on two nodes and attached by the command
––– input –––
chk() { grep -qE -- "$3" /var/log/manticore-$1/searchd.log && echo "yes: $2" || echo "no: $2"; }; chk 1 'prepared on 2 nodes' "bulk_import chunk [0-9]+ of table 't': prepared on 2 nodes"; chk 1 'attached by the command' "attach command finished in .* result 1"; chk 2 'receiver attached' "bulk_import chunk [0-9]+ of table 't': attached in .* files seqno 3$"
––– output –––
yes: prepared on 2 nodes
yes: attached by the command
yes: receiver attached
––– comment –––
HTTP: private on node 1 and Shared with shared=2 on node 2; every chunk goes through its own attach command, the rows are the same on every node
––– input –––
source /tmp/bc.sh; add th; gen() { for ((i=$1; i<=$2; i++)); do printf '{"insert":{"cluster":"v1","table":"th","id":%d,"doc":{"title":"title %d","v":%d}}}\n' "$i" "$i" "$i"; done; }; gen 1 1000 > /tmp/p.ndjson; gen 1001 3000 > /tmp/a.ndjson; gen 3001 5000 > /tmp/b.ndjson; printf '\n' > /tmp/commit.ndjson; post() { curl -sS -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$1/bulk?bulk_import=th$2" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @"$3" -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n'; }; echo ok
––– output –––
add th 0
ok
––– input –––
post 1308 '' /tmp/p.ndjson; source /tmp/bc.sh; st th
